    "ReconcileUnknownExecution": {
      "type": "object",
      "required": [
        "kind",
        "invocation",
        "reason"
      ],
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "description": "Private Core control write recording one immutable unknown disposition for an invocation whose Worker was permanently lost. It is not an Agent tool and appears in no MCP tool list. It carries no isolation field on purpose: Core reads the Connection and the Worker instance that took the work from the trusted dispatch record, and reads the generation that proves that instance can no longer claim or report from the Worker fence in force, so a request can neither assert isolation nor name a generation. Refused with fence_control_requires_no_connection when the request carries a Connection identity, not_permitted when the authenticated principal lacks the deployment-level governance role (a server-owned principal-to-roles table, never a header and never implied by holding a key), not_authorized when it lacks write access to this Board under the configured Board ACL, not_dispatchable when no trusted dispatch record names the invocation, already_reported when a trusted effect_confirmed or effect_failed already settled it, and worker_not_isolated when the fence has not advanced past the recorded generation. Recording is idempotent per invocation: a repeat writes nothing, bumps no revision, and replays the standing record with replay true. The fence only prevents this Board from accepting the old instance; it does not stop its process or undo external effects. The record certifies no outcome, applies no business effect, and closes no Case; completed still checks the unfiltered execution obligations even if model rules read this disposition, and the outcome stays unknown. It releases three gates for this invocation and nothing else. Two are Case gates of its attributed roots (Case Context section 5): a non-completed CloseCase, and PauseCase admission, where neither the host frontier nor the execution obligations count it while every other pause condition still applies (a Board whose live roots have all expired still refuses with board_draining). The third is Board-wide, so it also covers a Board-level invocation that has no attributed root: the quiescence check of an explicit UpdateBoardProgram migrate, whose reply lists the carried invocations in reconciledUnknownInvocations when the migration activates. Drain activation still requires every live root to be terminal. A completed CloseCase and a completed SealBoard still count it, and reconciliation releases no other obligation: verification, claimable action, review and evidence (material) obligations count exactly as they would without it. The pause and migration refinements are PSC 0.2.5 proposals adopted by the Java Core; the retiring Rust Core releases only the non-completed CloseCase gate.",
      "properties": {
        "kind": {
          "const": "ReconcileUnknownExecution"
        },
        "invocation": {
          "type": "string",
          "minLength": 1,
          "description": "The invocation whose execution outcome was never observed. It must already carry a trusted dispatch record on this Board."
        },
        "reason": {
          "type": "string",
          "minLength": 1,
          "description": "The operator's stated ground for the disposition, truncated to 240 UTF-16 units on the record. A disposition with no stated ground reads the same as a mistake, so an empty reason is a shape error."
        }
      }
    },
