{
  "format": "rulith-operations/1",
  "note": "Single source of truth for the operation surface. gen:operations emits op_registry_g.rs for the server and op_shape_g.rs for the protocol. Exhaustive Operation matches such as is_write_operation remain handwritten because compiler exhaustiveness is stronger than generated string tables; op_registry_conform.rs checks every sample against this registry. Array order is the byte-stable GetProtocolManifest advertisement order.",
  "fieldNote": "write identifies journaled writes; required entries are [field, type] parsed by gen:operations; manifest tags determine the native advertisement subsets. Model tool membership is defined only in protocol/mcp-surface.json. Operations name their targets on one shared graph; no Case envelope classification remains.",
  "operations": [
    {
      "kind": "GetProjection",
      "write": false,
      "required": [],
