        "nodeId": "N"
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "IngestObservation",
      "write": true,
      "required": [
        [
          "facts",
          "a"
        ]
      ],
      "manifest": [],
      "sample": {
        "kind": "IngestObservation",
        "facts": [
          {
            "predicate": "probe",
            "source": "plant-telemetry",
            "args": {}
          }
        ]
      },
      "note": "Every observation row states the Source that attests it: source is required per row, not per request, because one authenticated Connection legitimately carries several Sources. The advertised surface additionally requires a channel identity, and Boardd checks three separate things per row — that the row named a Source, that the server-owned Connection-to-Source registry says this Connection carries it, and that a channel_binding accredits that Source for that predicate. The grounding tier comes from that binding. Nothing is defaulted from the Connection: picking the line's only Source works until a second one is added, and on that day the weaker Source starts entering at the stronger one's tier with no reading anywhere changed."
    },
    {
      "kind": "RegisterPack",
      "write": true,
      "required": [
        [
          "packType",
          "s"
        ],
        [
          "pack",
          "p"
        ]
      ],
      "manifest": [],
      "sample": {
        "kind": "RegisterPack",
        "packType": "domain",
        "pack": {}
      },
      "note": "The advertised surface additionally requires an unlocked board and may_legislate authorization."
    },
    {
      "kind": "RemovePack",
      "write": true,
      "required": [
        [
          "packType",
          "s"
        ],
        [
          "name",
          "s"
        ],
        [
          "expectedDigest",
          "s"
        ]
      ],
      "manifest": [],
      "sample": {
        "kind": "RemovePack",
        "packType": "domain",
        "name": "verified-calculation",
        "expectedDigest": "sha256:current"
      },
      "note": "Governed CAS-pinned removal of one effective package. It queues behind open Cases and is advertised only when the caller may legislate and the law lock is open."
    },
    {
      "kind": "CreateBoard",
      "write": true,
      "required": [],
      "manifest": [],
      "sample": {
        "kind": "CreateBoard",
        "title": "t"
      },
      "note": "Never appears in a board Manifest because the board does not exist before this operation."
    },
    {
      "kind": "OpenCase",
      "agentVerb": true,
      "write": true,
      "required": [],
      "manifest": [],
      "sample": {
        "kind": "OpenCase",
        "caseType": "exploration"
      },
      "note": "Two public shapes and no third: {caseType, businessKey?} registers a new acceptance root, {caseId} returns to one. Mixed or empty is refused rather than resolved by precedence. The authority mints both the Case id and the acceptance root and returns them; root, caseId-on-create and expectedBoardSharedEpoch are retired inputs refused by name. Gateway-authorized admission (capabilityReleaseDigest, caseContractDigest, businessKeyDigest, commercialTermsDigest, maxExplorationBps, affinityKey) travels in the command envelope, not here. Shape validation lives in the parser because required[] cannot express two alternative shapes."
    },
    {
      "kind": "PauseCase",
      "write": true,
      "required": [
        [
          "caseId",
          "s"
        ],
        [
          "source",
          "s"
        ]
      ],
      "manifest": [],
      "sample": {
        "kind": "PauseCase",
        "caseId": "CASE_1",
        "source": "operator"
      },
      "note": "Names its Case explicitly: one shared graph has no current Case to read it from. source is a closed set (operator|policy) with no default — a guessed source files a human hold as one a policy may lift, or lets a policy manufacture a hold only a human can clear."
    },
    {
      "kind": "ResumeCase",
      "write": true,
      "required": [
        [
          "caseId",
          "s"
        ],
        [
          "source",
          "s"
        ]
      ],
      "manifest": [],
      "sample": {
        "kind": "ResumeCase",
        "caseId": "CASE_1",
        "source": "operator"
      },
      "note": "Lifts one hold of the named source only. The root stays paused while any other hold is in force; an operator does not lift a policy hold and a policy never lifts an operator one."
    },
    {
      "kind": "MaintainBoardShared",
      "write": true,
      "required": [
        [
          "operations",
          "a"
        ]
      ],
      "manifest": [],
      "sample": {
        "kind": "MaintainBoardShared",
        "operations": []
