      "note": "Verification reports carry exactly one result axis: an explicit outcome of satisfied, not_satisfied, or error. satisfied means the check ran and the condition holds; not_satisfied means the check ran normally but the business condition does not currently hold, so the same world is not retried; error means execution or backend failure and enters retry backoff. A verification report without outcome is bad_command. Action reports instead carry ok and require execution: the authenticated Connection injects the invocation, Action, Tool Contract, Source, Connection, Worker, Adapter, request, result, outcome, and timestamp chain; Boardd rejects a missing or mismatched chain before any effect write. The chain names the invocation, not a Case. execution.invocationId is read out of the dispatch grant the Worker returns unchanged, after the Connection has verified that grant was issued to this Worker, Connection and Board; it MUST NOT be copied from this report's id. Copying it would turn Boardd's comparison into an identity and let a grant earned by one invocation settle another. Boardd then requires that value to equal both this report's id and the trusted dispatch record that id names, so a report carrying some other invocation's grant is refused rather than flattened. Boardd verifies no signature of its own: the signing lives on the Connection's grant, and Boardd's side is Connection authentication plus field-by-field comparison against Board-owned state. Evidence reports carry material and a required source: the Board mints one collection order per Source accredited to attest that material, each naming its own, and the report must file under the same one. Boardd refuses a report that states no source rather than choosing from the reporting Connection, and refuses one that names a different Source than the order was issued to — otherwise a Connection could collect under a weak Source and file under a stronger one it also carries. Landed evidence rows are stamped at the tier bound to that (source, material) pair."
